K90 builtin: declare EVENT_SERVICES

SukiSU-Ultra builtin 70fa0e09 synced dispatch.c from official KernelSU
(#3800) which switches on EVENT_SERVICES, but kernel/include/uapi/supercall.h
still only has POST_FS_DATA / BOOT_COMPLETED / MODULE_MOUNTED. GKI
CONFIG_WERROR fails with undeclared identifier. Same DECLARE() style as
the rest of the builtin header. Skip once builtin ships EVENT_SERVICES=4.

--- a/kernel/include/uapi/supercall.h
+++ b/kernel/include/uapi/supercall.h
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 DECLARE(__u32, EVENT_POST_FS_DATA, 1);
 DECLARE(__u32, EVENT_BOOT_COMPLETED, 2);
 DECLARE(__u32, EVENT_MODULE_MOUNTED, 3);
+DECLARE(__u32, EVENT_SERVICES, 4);
 
 DECLARE(__u32, KSU_GET_INFO_FLAG_LKM, (1U << 0));
 DECLARE(__u32, KSU_GET_INFO_FLAG_MANAGER, (1U << 1));
